{
  "challenge": "C-004",
  "task": "Copy every value other than the chosen target into the output, preserving order.\n\nImplement `size_t remove_value(const int *values, size_t count, int target, int *out)`, returning how many values were copied. `out` has room for `count` integers. Empty input and removing all values produce an empty output. Input has at most 200 integers in -10000..10000; target is in the same range. Do not modify the input.\n\n## Examples\n\nInput: `[[2, 1, 2, 3], 2]` → output: `[1, 3]`.\nInput: `[[], 0]` → output: `[]`.\n",
  "language": "c",
  "file": "remove_value.c",
  "starter": "// TODO: implement the task.\n#include <stddef.h>\nsize_t remove_value(const int *values, size_t count, int target, int *out) { return 0; }\n",
  "entrypoint": "remove_value",
  "parameters": [
    "values",
    "target"
  ],
  "adapter": "#include \"mm_json.h\"\n#include <stdlib.h>\nsize_t remove_value(const int *, size_t, int, int *);\nmm_value *mm_call(const mm_value *args) {\n    const mm_value *list = mm_at(args, 0);\n    size_t n = mm_length(list);\n    int *a = calloc(n + 1, sizeof(int));\n    int *out = calloc(n + 1, sizeof(int));\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++)\n        a[i] = (int)mm_integer(mm_at(list, i));\n    size_t count = remove_value(a, n, (int)mm_integer(mm_at(args, 1)), out);\n    mm_value *r = mm_new_array();\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < count && i < n; i++)\n        mm_push(r, mm_new_integer(out[i]));\n    return r;\n}\n",
